/E (Controlling possession: At the core of De Zerbi's strategy is the concept of controlling possession. This isn't possession for the sake of it but a deliberate, methodical approach to dominate the game. By rationally occupying space, De Zerbi's teams spread the opposition thin, creating gaps that can be exploited. The use of short third-man passing combinations is central to this strategy, as it allows for quick, incisive plays that can break defensive lines. Player spatial awareness is critical; athletes under De Zerbi are adept at recognizing when to pass and when to drive forward with the ball, showcasing a level of decision-making that is both instinctive and deeply ingrained through rigorous training. Technical ability underpins this philosophy, ensuring players are equipped to execute De Zerbi's vision on the pitch.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
