/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (Brighton excels in playing in the transitional spaces between the midfield and defense lines, where they can use quick passes and movement to destabilize the structure. Brighton's style includes "automatic elements" which means the players are trained to perform certain actions reflexively based on specific triggers or scenarios. This results in a game that is fluid and rapid, minimizing the time and space the opposition has to react. This speed and synchronicity in both thought and action enhance their ability to seamlessly connect plays, often making their movements seem un-intuitive to opponents.)
